invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the comparison takes r + n modulo 2^384 for a second value of
  x, so r = x + 2^384 - n, which is in range for nearly every x,
  passes for a point whose x is not r modulo n. bin/p384_equiv_test
  builds that signature and wants 0.

--- old
    if (p384_wide_add_raw(r_plus_n, r, p384_wide_modn.m) != 0 ||
        p384_wide_compare(r_plus_n, p384_wide_modp.m) >= 0) {
--- new
    (void)p384_wide_add_raw(r_plus_n, r, p384_wide_modn.m);
    if (p384_wide_compare(r_plus_n, p384_wide_modp.m) >= 0) {
